<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The platform theme. It owns only the window before Compose draws — every colour the user actually
  sees comes from dev.rsm.ui.theme.RsmTheme.

  Two things it must still get right:

    * windowBackground. This is the first frame on a cold start, so a light value here produces a
      white flash before the dark Compose surface appears. res/values-night/ overrides both this
      file and colors.xml, which is why the style is duplicated there rather than parented on a
      DayNight theme: appcompat and material-components are not dependencies (this is pure Compose
      on a plain ComponentActivity), and the platform's own DayNight variants are DeviceDefault-only.

    * No edge-to-edge opt-out. targetSdk is 37, where the system draws the app behind the status and
      navigation bars whether or not it asks to. The fix for content landing under the notification
      bar is to inset the content — MainActivity calls enableEdgeToEdge() and the Scaffold/TopAppBar
      apply the insets — NOT to set android:windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement, which is a temporary
      compatibility flag the platform is removing.

  statusBarColor and navigationBarColor are deliberately absent: they are no-ops from API 35 on, and
  below that enableEdgeToEdge() sets them itself.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Rsm" parent="android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/window_background</item>
    </style>
</resources>
